# Start a new prototype

Help the designer start a prototype. Speak in terms of screens and states, never file paths.

1. Ask what the prototype is about in one sentence, and which screens or states it needs
   (for example: the list, an empty list, an error). Ask who uses it (the roles) if that is unclear.
2. Pick a short name for it: lowercase words joined by dashes, like `checkout-redesign`. Confirm it
   with the designer.
3. Run `npm run design-space:new -- <name>` from the design space folder. It creates your own
   working copy of the project and a starter prototype to build on. If it refuses the name or says
   the prototype already exists, pick another name.
4. Build the first version of the screens the designer described, using only real product
   components and tokens, and cover loading, empty, error and success states. Follow the rules in
   `AGENTS.md`.
5. Tell the designer, in plain words, what screens now exist and which states each one has.

Next step: run `design-space-preview` to look at it in the browser.
